307|We imagine gorgeous hotels,|
308|travel and meeting people.|
309|But we sometimes forget the irregular hours,|
310|difficult customers|
311|or tiring trips.|
312|Exactly. Or being a chef!|
313|We see the beautiful dishes,|
314|but rarely the long hours|
315|standing in a kitchen.|
316|That's why it's important|
317|to discover the reality of a job|
318|before making a big decision.|
319|You know, a friend of mine dreamed|B={"mode":"timeline","bg":"liege","title":"Le rêve de son amie","items":[{"label":"le rêve","text":"une boutique de fleurs","at":1},{"label":"d'abord","text":"chez une fleuriste","at":8},{"label":"la réalité","text":"se lever très tôt","at":12}]}
320|of opening a flower shop.|
321|Oh, how charming!|
322|Yes. She imagined spending her days|
323|surrounded by gorgeous flowers,|
324|making bouquets for her customers.|
325|And did she open her shop?|
326|Not right away.|
327|She first worked for a few weeks|
328|at a florist's to discover the job.|
329|That was a very good idea.|
330|Yes. And she discovered|
331|that you had to get up very early,|
332|carry boxes, handle orders|
333|and sometimes work very long days.|BE
334|So the job was more demanding|e=idee
335|than she imagined.|
336|Exactly. She still loved flowers,|
337|but she understood she preferred|
338|creating arrangements for events|
339|rather than running a shop every day.|
340|That's an excellent example.|
341|Sometimes, trying an activity helps us|
342|better understand what we really want.|
343|Yes. And that doesn't mean|
344|our dream was ridiculous.|
345|We simply learned|
346|something new.|
347|Exactly.|
348|That's why it can be useful|
349|to talk with professionals,|
350|take a short course|
351|or do an internship.|
352|Because a job isn't just its image.|e=idee
353|Exactly. You also have to imagine|
354|a normal day in that profession.|
355|Not just the first day,|
356|when everything is new and exciting.|
357|Exactly. Imagine an ordinary Tuesday,|e=question
358|after six months on the job.|
359|Do the daily tasks|
360|still interest you?|
361|Ah, that question is very useful.|
362|Because even an exciting job|
363|has ordinary days.|
364|And sometimes, difficult days.|
365|You know, that brings us|
366|to talk about personality.|
367|Yes. Because a job that's ideal for one person|
368|can be very hard for another.|
369|For example, some people love|
370|speaking in front of an audience.|
371|Whereas others|
372|prefer to work quietly,|
373|in a calmer environment.|
374|Me, I like communicating,|
375|but I wouldn't want to spend|
376|my whole day on the phone.|i=telephone:le téléphone
377|And I like organising ideas|
