541|Now, I'd like to talk about|
542|a few very useful expressions|
543|for our listeners.|
544|Great idea!|e=idee
545|Because talking about your work|
546|and your career plans|
547|is a common topic|
548|in French conversations.|
549|For example, to ask|
550|someone's job, you can say:|
551|"What do you do for a living?"|
552|Or: "What field|
553|do you work in?"|
554|And to talk about your ambitions, you can say:|
555|"I'd like to work in tourism."|
556|Or: "My dream would be to become an architect."|
557|Exactly.|
558|And if you're not sure of your choice yet,|
559|you can say:|
560|"I'm still thinking about|
561|my career path."|
562|"Career guidance"|
563|is looking for a job|
564|or a field that suits us.|
565|Very good. Now, let's review|
566|some natural expressions.|
567|Let's start with "trouver sa voie".|B={"mode":"compare","bg":"liege","title":"trouver ou changer ?","left":{"head":"trouver sa voie","sub":"découvrir sa direction","items":[{"text":"une direction qui nous correspond","at":2},{"text":"« dans le design »","at":5}]},"right":{"head":"changer de voie","sub":"une nouvelle direction","items":[{"text":"dans ses études","at":8},{"text":"dans sa carrière","at":8}]}}
568|"Trouver sa voie" means discovering|
569|a professional or personal direction|
570|that suits us.|
571|For example: "After several experiences,|
572|she found her path in design."|
573|Second expression: "changer de voie".|
574|It means choosing a new direction,|
575|often in your studies or career.|
576|For example:|
577|"After a few years in sales,|
578|he decided to change direction."|BE
579|Third expression:|B={"mode":"word","bg":"carnet","note":"= se sentir bien, progresser, trouver de la satisfaction"}
580|"to flourish in your work".|
581|It means feeling good,|
582|growing and finding satisfaction|
583|in your professional activity.|
584|For example: "She flourishes in her job|
585|because she likes helping others."|BE
586|Fourth expression:|
587|"to have a sense of something".|
588|It describes an ability|
589|or a particular quality.|
590|For example: "He has a knack for organising."|
591|Or: "She's good with people."|
592|Fifth expression: "gagner sa vie".|
593|It means earning the money you need|
594|to live through your work.|
595|For example: "He'd like to earn a living|
596|doing photography."|
597|And our last expression:|
598|"se reconvertir".|
599|"Se reconvertir" means|
600|changing job or professional field|
601|after already working in another sector.|
602|For example:|
603|"After ten years in finance, she decided|
604|to retrain as a teacher."|
605|There you go, six very useful expressions|
606|to talk about work and the future.|
607|And now, let's see how to make|
608|some sentences sound more natural in French.|
